{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0176ngiGjgzMrWa7V7yfw4ba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# microtags\n2\t\n3\tA helper for building custom elements that hydrate server-rendered HTML.\n4\tThe browser downloads behaviour only; markup is authored once and rendered\n5\ton the server.\n6\t\n7\t## Language\n8\t\n9\t### Defining a component\n10\t\n11\t**Component**:\n12\tA custom element defined through the builder chain. It carries behaviour\n13\tand, when it has a render link, its own markup.\n14\t_Avoid_: widget, element (ambiguous with the host instance)\n15\t\n16\t**Tag name**:\n17\tThe custom element name a component is registered under, such as\n18\t`my-counter`. Exposed on the class as `TAG`.\n19\t_Avoid_: element name, selector\n20\t\n21\t**Builder chain**:\n22\tThe sequence of calls that defines a component, starting at `define` and\n23\tending at `setup`.\n24\t_Avoid_: pipeline, config\n25\t\n26\t**Link**:\n27\tOne call in the builder chain: `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts`,\n28\tor `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n29\t_Avoid_: step, method (in prose)\n30\t\n31\t**Prop**:\n32\tA named input declared with `withProps`. Inside `setup` it is a signal.\n33\tAn attribute-backed prop is read from the host's HTML attribute of the same\n34\tname; a property-only prop is set from JavaScript only. Every prop also has\n35\ta property accessor on the host: assigning a plain value writes the prop,\n36\tand assigning a signal makes the prop read through to that signal\n37\t(`bindProp` does this with the signal's type checked). Once a\n38\tsignal is assigned, the attribute is no longer updated and does not\n39\treflect the current value. A bound prop is read-only inside the\n40\tcomponent: writing it from `setup` throws, so the component emits an\n41\tevent instead.\n42\t_Avoid_: attribute (that is the HTML side of a prop), input, option\n43\t\n44\t**Coercer**:\n45\tA function that turns a raw attribute string, or its absence, into a typed\n46\tprop value. The four builtins are `number`, `string`, `boolean`, `json`.\n47\t_Avoid_: parser, validator\n48\t\n49\t**Schema prop**:\n50\tA prop validated by a Standard Schema object rather than a builtin coercer.\n51\tA failed validation yields `undefined`.\n52\t_Avoid_: validated prop, custom prop\n53\t\n54\t**Ref**:\n55\tA child element the component declares with `withRefs` and resolves when\n56\tthe host connects, after an empty host with a kept render link is\n57\trendered. By default a ref is found by its `data-ref` attribute.\n58\t_Avoid_: query, element ref, handle\n59\t\n60\t**Statics**:\n61\tThe values exposed on a component's class for use outside the browser:\n62\t`TAG`, `refs`, `render`, `renderParts`, and `props`.\n63\t_Avoid_: metadata, class properties\n64\t\n65\t### Running a component\n66\t\n67\t**Host**:\n68\tThe custom element instance a component's behaviour is attached to. Its\n69\tchildren are light DOM, never a shadow root.\n70\t_Avoid_: root, wrapper, container\n71\t\n72\t**Setup**:\n73\tThe function run once per host when it connects, after required provided\n74\tcontexts are available, an empty host with a kept render link is\n75\trendered, and refs resolve. Its cleanups run a microtask\n76\tafter the host disconnects, and only if it is still disconnected, so a\n77\thost moved within one tick keeps its setup and state.\n78\t_Avoid_: init, mount, constructor\n79\t\n80\t**Setup context**:\n81\tThe object handed to `setup`, carrying the host, prop signals, resolved\n82\trefs, provided context values, and lifecycle helpers.\n83\t_Avoid_: bare \"context\", ctx (in prose)\n84\t\n85\t**Provided context**:\n86\tA value published by an ancestor host and read by descendants that opt in\n87\twith `withContexts` or `consume`. Reactive: consumers re-run when the\n88\tprovider updates.\n89\t_Avoid_: bare \"context\", store, global\n90\t\n91\t**Hydration**:\n92\tAttaching behaviour to markup that already exists in the document. At the\n93\tcomponent level this happens when the class is registered; at the page\n94\tlevel the browser rebuilds the serialized state and mounts the same page\n95\tover the server-rendered DOM, adopting it.\n96\t_Avoid_: mounting, rendering, upgrading (the browser's term for the\n97\tmechanism, not the intent)\n98\t\n99\t### Rendering markup\n100\t\n101\t**Render function**:\n102\tThe author-supplied function given to the `render` link. It returns the\n103\thost's inner HTML as a string or markup; the library wraps it in the host tag.\n104\t_Avoid_: template, view\n105\t\n106\t**Render context**:\n107\tThe object handed to the render function: plain prop values, the ref name\n108\tmap, the tag name, and caller-supplied children and attrs. Distinct from\n109\tthe setup context and from provided context.\n110\t_Avoid_: bare \"context\", props (it is more than props)\n111\t\n112\t**Host tag**:\n113\tThe opening and closing markup of the host, with its serialized\n114\tattributes, emitted around the render function's output.\n115\t_Avoid_: wrapper, outer HTML\n116\t\n117\t**Render parts**:\n118\tThe same server render as the `render` static, split into the host tag\n119\tname, the serialized (unescaped) host attributes, and the inner HTML.\n120\tReturned by the `renderParts` static so another renderer can build the\n121\thost tag itself.\n122\t_Avoid_: fragments, pieces\n123\t\n124\t**Markup**:\n125\tThe opaque value `html`, `h`, and `raw` return (`Markup`). On the server\n126\t`String(m)` yields the HTML; in the browser it also describes the nodes\n127\tmount creates or adopts.\n128\t_Avoid_: template (that is the HTML element), HTML string\n129\t\n130\t**Reactive region**:\n131\tA signal or function in a child-position hole. The server evaluates it\n132\tonce and wraps its output in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->` comment markers;\n133\tthe browser re-evaluates it and morphs the nodes between the markers,\n134\tmatching children by `key`, else by position and tag name. Children\n135\tpassed to a component are not a region: they open with their own\n136\t`<!--[c-->` marker (closed by `<!--]-->`), so the browser can tell them\n137\tfrom regions in the component's own render.\n138\t_Avoid_: block, slot, island\n139\t\n140\t**Mount**:\n141\tThe browser templater's `mount(container, markup)`. It adopts the\n142\tcontainer's children when there are any, otherwise creates the nodes, and\n143\treturns a dispose function that stops effects and removes listeners.\n144\t_Avoid_: render (that is the link), hydrate (that is the intent)\n145\t\n146\t**Adopt**:\n147\tWalking markup against DOM that already exists and binding props,\n148\tattributes, listeners, and regions to it without creating nodes. It never\n149\tdescends into a host's own markup, only into its marked children range.\n150\t_Avoid_: reuse, claim\n151\t\n152\t**Server render**:\n153\tProducing a component's or page's markup as a string outside the browser.\n154\t\"SSR\" is an accepted abbreviation.\n155\t_Avoid_: pre-render, static render\n156\t\n157\t**Client-rendered component**:\n158\tA component whose render link is kept in the browser bundle so it can\n159\tproduce its own markup after page load. A page asks for the client\n160\trender by inserting an empty host; core renders it before refs resolve.\n161\t_Avoid_: dynamic component, lazy component\n162\t\n163\t**Templater**:\n164\tThe `html` tagged template that composes a page from plain tags and\n165\tcomponents, escaping interpolated strings and expanding nested components.\n166\tIt returns markup. The same import resolves to a server build and a\n167\tbrowser build; the browser build also binds signals, listeners, and\n168\treactive regions, and exports mount.\n169\t_Avoid_: template engine, template (that is the HTML element below)\n170\t\n171\t**Template**:\n172\tThe native `<template>` HTML element that `render` and `renderList` from\n173\tthe DOM helpers clone rows from. Unrelated to the templater.\n174\t_Avoid_: template string, partial\n175\t\n176\t**Trusted string**:\n177\tContent the templater inserts without escaping. Markup (the output of the\n178\ttemplater and of `raw`) and the output of a render function are trusted;\n179\tevery other interpolated string is escaped. Nesting markup never\n180\tdouble-escapes it.\n181\t_Avoid_: safe string, raw HTML (that is the function name)\n182\t\n183\t### Building for the client\n184\t\n185\t**Strip**:\n186\tRemoving a component's render link from client code at build time so the\n187\tbrowser does not download markup.\n188\t_Avoid_: tree-shake (that is the bundler's own dead-code pass), prune\n189\t\n190\t**Keep**:\n191\tAn opt-out from stripping, declared in source with `client: true` or at\n192\tbuild time by tag name.\n193\t_Avoid_: preserve, whitelist\n194\t\n195\t**Cascade**:\n196\tAfter stripping, removing the imports and top-level declarations that only\n197\tthe stripped code used, repeated until nothing more is removed.\n198\t_Avoid_: dead-code elimination, tree-shake\n199\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f913a53-0f10-4f84-aeba-59a85cf43fa6","uuid":"91466534-ae6f-405d-9b7c-fcedc5a5ef03","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:34:35.325Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.form-associated-02-form-associated-link-and-internals/CONTEXT.md","content":"# microtags\n\nA helper for building custom elements that hydrate server-rendered HTML.\nThe browser downloads behaviour only; markup is authored once and rendered\non the server.\n\n## Language\n\n### Defining a component\n\n**Component**:\nA custom element defined through the builder chain. It carries behaviour\nand, when it has a render link, its own markup.\n_Avoid_: widget, element (ambiguous with the host instance)\n\n**Tag name**:\nThe custom element name a component is registered under, such as\n`my-counter`. Exposed on the class as `TAG`.\n_Avoid_: element name, selector\n\n**Builder chain**:\nThe sequence of calls that defines a component, starting at `define` and\nending at `setup`.\n_Avoid_: pipeline, config\n\n**Link**:\nOne call in the builder chain: `withProps`, `withRefs`, `withContexts`,\nor `render`. `setup` is the terminal link.\n_Avoid_: step, method (in prose)\n\n**Prop**:\nA named input declared with `withProps`. Inside `setup` it is a signal.\nAn attribute-backed prop is read from the host's HTML attribute of the same\nname; a property-only prop is set from JavaScript only. Every prop also has\na property accessor on the host: assigning a plain value writes the prop,\nand assigning a signal makes the prop read through to that signal\n(`bindProp` does this with the signal's type checked). Once a\nsignal is assigned, the attribute is no longer updated and does not\nreflect the current value. A bound prop is read-only inside the\ncomponent: writing it from `setup` throws, so the component emits an\nevent instead.\n_Avoid_: attribute (that is the HTML side of a prop), input, option\n\n**Coercer**:\nA function that turns a raw attribute string, or its absence, into a typed\nprop value. The four builtins are `number`, `string`, `boolean`, `json`.\n_Avoid_: parser, validator\n\n**Schema prop**:\nA prop validated by a Standard Schema object rather than a builtin coercer.\nA failed validation yields `undefined`.\n_Avoid_: validated prop, custom prop\n\n**Ref**:\nA child element the component declares with `withRefs` and resolves when\nthe host connects, after an empty host with a kept render link is\nrendered. By default a ref is found by its `data-ref` attribute.\n_Avoid_: query, element ref, handle\n\n**Statics**:\nThe values exposed on a component's class for use outside the browser:\n`TAG`, `refs`, `render`, `renderParts`, and `props`.\n_Avoid_: metadata, class properties\n\n### Running a component\n\n**Host**:\nThe custom element instance a component's behaviour is attached to. Its\nchildren are light DOM, never a shadow root.\n_Avoid_: root, wrapper, container\n\n**Setup**:\nThe function run once per host when it connects, after required provided\ncontexts are available, an empty host with a kept render link is\nrendered, and refs resolve. Its cleanups run a microtask\nafter the host disconnects, and only if it is still disconnected, so a\nhost moved within one tick keeps its setup and state.\n_Avoid_: init, mount, constructor\n\n**Setup context**:\nThe object handed to `setup`, carrying the host, prop signals, resolved\nrefs, provided context values, and lifecycle helpers.\n_Avoid_: bare \"context\", ctx (in prose)\n\n**Provided context**:\nA value published by an ancestor host and read by descendants that opt in\nwith `withContexts` or `consume`. Reactive: consumers re-run when the\nprovider updates.\n_Avoid_: bare \"context\", store, global\n\n**Hydration**:\nAttaching behaviour to markup that already exists in the document. At the\ncomponent level this happens when the class is registered; at the page\nlevel the browser rebuilds the serialized state and mounts the same page\nover the server-rendered DOM, adopting it.\n_Avoid_: mounting, rendering, upgrading (the browser's term for the\nmechanism, not the intent)\n\n### Rendering markup\n\n**Render function**:\nThe author-supplied function given to the `render` link. It returns the\nhost's inner HTML as a string or markup; the library wraps it in the host tag.\n_Avoid_: template, view\n\n**Render context**:\nThe object handed to the render function: plain prop values, the ref name\nmap, the tag name, and caller-supplied children and attrs. Distinct from\nthe setup context and from provided context.\n_Avoid_: bare \"context\", props (it is more than props)\n\n**Host tag**:\nThe opening and closing markup of the host, with its serialized\nattributes, emitted around the render function's output.\n_Avoid_: wrapper, outer HTML\n\n**Render parts**:\nThe same server render as the `render` static, split into the host tag\nname, the serialized (unescaped) host attributes, and the inner HTML.\nReturned by the `renderParts` static so another renderer can build the\nhost tag itself.\n_Avoid_: fragments, pieces\n\n**Markup**:\nThe opaque value `html`, `h`, and `raw` return (`Markup`). On the server\n`String(m)` yields the HTML; in the browser it also describes the nodes\nmount creates or adopts.\n_Avoid_: template (that is the HTML element), HTML string\n\n**Reactive region**:\nA signal or function in a child-position hole. The server evaluates it\nonce and wraps its output in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->` comment markers;\nthe browser re-evaluates it and morphs the nodes between the markers,\nmatching children by `key`, else by position and tag name. Children\npassed to a component are not a region: they open with their own\n`<!--[c-->` marker (closed by `<!--]-->`), so the browser can tell them\nfrom regions in the component's own render.\n_Avoid_: block, slot, island\n\n**Mount**:\nThe browser templater's `mount(container, markup)`. It adopts the\ncontainer's children when there are any, otherwise creates the nodes, and\nreturns a dispose function that stops effects and removes listeners.\n_Avoid_: render (that is the link), hydrate (that is the intent)\n\n**Adopt**:\nWalking markup against DOM that already exists and binding props,\nattributes, listeners, and regions to it without creating nodes. It never\ndescends into a host's own markup, only into its marked children range.\n_Avoid_: reuse, claim\n\n**Server render**:\nProducing a component's or page's markup as a string outside the browser.\n\"SSR\" is an accepted abbreviation.\n_Avoid_: pre-render, static render\n\n**Client-rendered component**:\nA component whose render link is kept in the browser bundle so it can\nproduce its own markup after page load. A page asks for the client\nrender by inserting an empty host; core renders it before refs resolve.\n_Avoid_: dynamic component, lazy component\n\n**Templater**:\nThe `html` tagged template that composes a page from plain tags and\ncomponents, escaping interpolated strings and expanding nested components.\nIt returns markup. The same import resolves to a server build and a\nbrowser build; the browser build also binds signals, listeners, and\nreactive regions, and exports mount.\n_Avoid_: template engine, template (that is the HTML element below)\n\n**Template**:\nThe native `<template>` HTML element that `render` and `renderList` from\nthe DOM helpers clone rows from. Unrelated to the templater.\n_Avoid_: template string, partial\n\n**Trusted string**:\nContent the templater inserts without escaping. Markup (the output of the\ntemplater and of `raw`) and the output of a render function are trusted;\nevery other interpolated string is escaped. Nesting markup never\ndouble-escapes it.\n_Avoid_: safe string, raw HTML (that is the function name)\n\n### Building for the client\n\n**Strip**:\nRemoving a component's render link from client code at build time so the\nbrowser does not download markup.\n_Avoid_: tree-shake (that is the bundler's own dead-code pass), prune\n\n**Keep**:\nAn opt-out from stripping, declared in source with `client: true` or at\nbuild time by tag name.\n_Avoid_: preserve, whitelist\n\n**Cascade**:\nAfter stripping, removing the imports and top-level declarations that only\nthe stripped code used, repeated until nothing more is removed.\n_Avoid_: dead-code elimination, tree-shake\n","numLines":199,"startLine":1,"totalLines":199}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0176ngiGjgzMrWa7V7yfw4ba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
