{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BdsvVCpeNbmxAamJ9RMQNZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ADR-011: Core renders an empty host with a kept render link\n2\t\n3\t**Date:** 2026-11-10\n4\t\n5\t**Status:** Accepted\n6\t\n7\t**Amends:** [ADR-010][adr-010]\n8\t\n9\t**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size), [ADR-009][adr-009]\n10\t(render links and render support)\n11\t\n12\t## Context\n13\t\n14\tA client-rendered component keeps its render link in the browser\n15\tbundle so it can produce its own markup after page load. A page asks\n16\tfor that by inserting an empty host: `document.createElement`,\n17\t`innerHTML`, or hand-written `<number-input></number-input>`.\n18\t\n19\tCore resolved refs against the host before setup ran, and it never\n20\trendered into the host. For an empty host every `r.one` ref was\n21\tmissing, so connect threw \"missing refs\" and setup never ran. The\n22\tworkaround in `../components` had three parts, copied into every\n23\tclient-rendered component: declare every ref with `r.all` so\n24\tresolution cannot throw, render the host's inner HTML in setup from\n25\t`host.constructor.renderParts`, then look each element up again by\n26\t`data-ref` because the setup context's refs were resolved before the\n27\trender. The ref types were wrong (arrays for single elements), the\n28\tsetup context's `refs` were stale, and setup had two code paths.\n29\t\n30\t## Decision\n31\t\n32\tWhen a host connects empty and its class has a `renderParts` static,\n33\tcore writes the parts' `html` into the host, then resolves refs, then\n34\truns setup.\n35\t\n36\t- **Ordering.** The render runs in the factory's connect path, after\n37\t  the required provided contexts are available and immediately before\n38\t  refs are resolved. A host waiting on a context stays empty until\n39\t  setup is about to run.\n40\t- **Empty.** No element children, no comments and no non-whitespace\n41\t  text (the inner HTML is whitespace). A host with any element child,\n42\t  comment or text is treated as server markup and left alone (the\n43\t  hydration case), including a host the page filled with its own\n44\t  children. Comments count because a templater or server host whose\n45\t  children region is empty holds only its `<!--[c-->`/`<!--[-->`\n46\t  markers, and those must survive for the region to work.\n47\t- **Input.** The current value of every declared prop, read through\n48\t  the host's accessors after attributes are applied, so attributes,\n49\t  properties set before upgrade and bound signals all reach the\n50\t  render. No children and no extra attrs."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f913a53-0f10-4f84-aeba-59a85cf43fa6","uuid":"01e4ee78-d1a5-43c5-90f1-033d637b2983","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:39:30.192Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.form-associated-02-form-associated-link-and-internals/docs/adr/ADR-011-core-renders-empty-host.md","content":"# ADR-011: Core renders an empty host with a kept render link\n\n**Date:** 2026-11-10\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n**Amends:** [ADR-010][adr-010]\n\n**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size), [ADR-009][adr-009]\n(render links and render support)\n\n## Context\n\nA client-rendered component keeps its render link in the browser\nbundle so it can produce its own markup after page load. A page asks\nfor that by inserting an empty host: `document.createElement`,\n`innerHTML`, or hand-written `<number-input></number-input>`.\n\nCore resolved refs against the host before setup ran, and it never\nrendered into the host. For an empty host every `r.one` ref was\nmissing, so connect threw \"missing refs\" and setup never ran. The\nworkaround in `../components` had three parts, copied into every\nclient-rendered component: declare every ref with `r.all` so\nresolution cannot throw, render the host's inner HTML in setup from\n`host.constructor.renderParts`, then look each element up again by\n`data-ref` because the setup context's refs were resolved before the\nrender. The ref types were wrong (arrays for single elements), the\nsetup context's `refs` were stale, and setup had two code paths.\n\n## Decision\n\nWhen a host connects empty and its class has a `renderParts` static,\ncore writes the parts' `html` into the host, then resolves refs, then\nruns setup.\n\n- **Ordering.** The render runs in the factory's connect path, after\n  the required provided contexts are available and immediately before\n  refs are resolved. A host waiting on a context stays empty until\n  setup is about to run.\n- **Empty.** No element children, no comments and no non-whitespace\n  text (the inner HTML is whitespace). A host with any element child,\n  comment or text is treated as server markup and left alone (the\n  hydration case), including a host the page filled with its own\n  children. Comments count because a templater or server host whose\n  children region is empty holds only its `<!--[c-->`/`<!--[-->`\n  markers, and those must survive for the region to work.\n- **Input.** The current value of every declared prop, read through\n  the host's accessors after attributes are applied, so attributes,\n  properties set before upgrade and bound signals all reach the\n  render. No children and no extra attrs.","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BdsvVCpeNbmxAamJ9RMQNZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
